    "body": "One thing I don't like is that lines 247 and 249 are perfectly correlated, but from this part of the code they look like they are not. We can only have either best count or best probability, right?\r\n\r\nIn general, I am wondering if we should have this difference between count and probability at the level of the logger / vqa_object ... or if it maybe would be easier to use the same generic name internally, and change it then only at the end when the results are given back to the user. \r\n\r\nThe advantage is that we would be removing all if/else statements throughout the code and pushing all of them into only a place. \r\n\r\nDo we feel this could help with clarity? ",
    "created_at": "2022-06-07T06:39:33Z",
