    "body": "The main reason for differentiating between counts and probability is that the backends could only produce one result or the other. It was done so to avoid confusion on the types of results different backends could return. (Since the returned type in both scenarios are dictionaries.)\r\n\r\nIf we are looking for a better way to have the results be returned from the backend, and not have the separation at the Logger Level. An alternative that would result in a much cleaner solution would be to create output classes. Instead of returning a dictionary, we return an object of type `Counts` or `Probability` from the backend. These objects can then be recorded under some common attribute named `result` of the Logger Class. I believe this should help remove the if/else statements mentioned for the most part.",
    "created_at": "2022-06-07T16:59:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-07T16:59:44Z",
